      "deciding_condition": "internal_fourier_number",
      "field_revised": "expected_verdict",
      "adjudication_basis": "internal_fourier_number is a CONSERVATIVE SCREEN. The rule that decides it is what the criterion OBSERVED when it failed, not how confident the bound is and not how conventional its threshold is. Under the floor the horizon ran out before the one-term approximation could be compared to anything, so the criterion observed nothing: there is no evidence for the model and none against it. NOT_SUPPORTED asserts evidence against a design; these cases had none to assert, so the honest expected verdict is INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE.",
      "independent_violation_search": "Of the 70 hard cases whose ground truth names internal_fourier_number as the catcher and expected NOT_SUPPORTED, each was run and every model's assessment in every report was inspected for a condition that was evaluated and failed. 47 have one -- operating_temperature_utilization (40), reference_temperature_utilization (34), radiation_to_convection_ratio (3) -- and KEEP NOT_SUPPORTED. The 23 below have an empty `violated` across every model in every report.",
